  18:common/prog/ped_fw/timer/system_timer.c **** /** \file
  19:common/prog/ped_fw/timer/system_timer.c ****  *
  20:common/prog/ped_fw/timer/system_timer.c ****  *  \brief    Implementation of STIM.
  21:common/prog/ped_fw/timer/system_timer.c ****  *
  22:common/prog/ped_fw/timer/system_timer.c ****  *  \details  System timer library serves for single or periodic time
  23:common/prog/ped_fw/timer/system_timer.c ****  *            measurement and callback execution with resolution down to one
  24:common/prog/ped_fw/timer/system_timer.c ****  *            millisecond. System timer library contains two types of execution
  25:common/prog/ped_fw/timer/system_timer.c ****  *            handlers, interrupt handler and scheduler handler.
  26:common/prog/ped_fw/timer/system_timer.c ****  *
  27:common/prog/ped_fw/timer/system_timer.c ****  *            Scheduler handler is used for processing of less accurate timers.
  28:common/prog/ped_fw/timer/system_timer.c ****  *            Accuracy of these timers is given by time period of execution of
  29:common/prog/ped_fw/timer/system_timer.c ****  *            this handler. If accuracy of these timers is not sufficient, then
  30:common/prog/ped_fw/timer/system_timer.c ****  *            interrupt based timers (see next section) should be used instead.
  31:common/prog/ped_fw/timer/system_timer.c ****  *
  32:common/prog/ped_fw/timer/system_timer.c ****  *            Interrupt handler is called from hardware timer interrupt service
ARM GAS  C:\Users\SX2605~1.HOD\AppData\Local\Temp\ccB2s30X.s 			page 2


  33:common/prog/ped_fw/timer/system_timer.c ****  *            routine with period of integer value in milliseconds. This
  34:common/prog/ped_fw/timer/system_timer.c ****  *            handler is used for base time update and for processing of
  35:common/prog/ped_fw/timer/system_timer.c ****  *            accurate interrupt base timers (including callback execution).
  36:common/prog/ped_fw/timer/system_timer.c ****  *            For all ARM Cortex-M micro controllers, SysTick timer is used by
  37:common/prog/ped_fw/timer/system_timer.c ****  *            default for this purpose.
  38:common/prog/ped_fw/timer/system_timer.c ****  *
  39:common/prog/ped_fw/timer/system_timer.c ****  *            Interrupt based timers should only be used if really necessary,
  40:common/prog/ped_fw/timer/system_timer.c ****  *            and respective callback functions should be kept as light as
  41:common/prog/ped_fw/timer/system_timer.c ****  *            possible. Otherwise they can have impact on other real-time
  42:common/prog/ped_fw/timer/system_timer.c ****  *            functions (UART/DBus handling, RTOS scheduling, ...)
  43:common/prog/ped_fw/timer/system_timer.c ****  *
  44:common/prog/ped_fw/timer/system_timer.c ****  */
  45:common/prog/ped_fw/timer/system_timer.c **** 
